pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test (wrong verdict): found by the sweep that followed the
% `fresh_right` and `contradiction_proven` defects, and the same shape -- a
% premise trusted to mean something the code never establishes.
%
% The constraints a `scope` introduces are the loaded order's SPECIFICATION,
% derived inside `def_order` from the EMPTY formula. They are premises about
% the order's auxiliary variables and are a conservative extension of the
% current database only while those auxiliary variables are unconstrained in
% it. Nothing established that. `checker::validate_aux_var` checks `$`-prefixed
% names against the active order, but before any `load_order` there is no
% active order and the check passes vacuously, so the `red` below puts
% `+1 ~$q >= 1` into the database for a variable that the order then declares
% as `aux`. Inside `scope leq` / `scope geq` the specification contributes
% `+1 $q >= 1`, which contradicts it, and every proofgoal in the scope is
% discharged by `rup >= 1` against a contradiction that has nothing to do with
% the goal. `dom` then added `+1 ~x1 >= 1` for free and the formula, which
% `x1 = 1, x2 = 0` satisfies, verified as `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE`.
%
% `ScopeRule` now refuses to introduce specification premises while any of the
% order's auxiliary variables occurs in the database. A `scope` over an order
% whose auxiliary variables really are fresh is unaffected -- see
% correct/version3/dominance_with_aux_vars, which opens both scopes.
f 2;
red +1 ~$q >= 1 : $q -> 0 ;
def_order o
  vars
    left u1;
    right v1;
    aux $q;
  end;
  spec
    red +1 $q >= 1 : $q -> 1;
  end;
  def
    +1 ~u1 +1 v1 >= 1;
  end;
  transitivity
    vars
      fresh_right w1;
      fresh_aux_1 $b1;
      fresh_aux_2 $c1;
    end;
    proof
      proofgoal #1
        rup >= 1;
      qed;
    qed;
  end;
end;
load_order o x1;
dom +1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 : subproof
  scope leq
    proofgoal #1
      rup >= 1;
    qed;
  end scope;
  scope geq
    proofgoal #2
      rup >= 1;
    qed;
  end scope;
qed;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : -1;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
